---
alwaysApply: true
---

# Android Instructions

// Complete Flutter Architecture Guide & Rules (.cursorrules)

This file serves as both a configuration for linting/automation and as the

// single source of truth for the architectural standards of this project
// 1. PHILOSOPHY: MVVM + CLEAN ARCHITECTURE
//
// - Clean Architecture: Dependencies must only point inwards
// (Presentation -> Domain <- Data). The Domain (business logic) is the core
// and knows nothing about UI or data sources
// - MVVM (Model-View-ViewModel): The Presentation layer is split
// - View (Pages/Widgets): The UI. Dumb and reactive
// - ViewModel (Bloc/Cubit): The bridge. Manages UI state and talks to the Domain
// - Modularity: The app is built as a collection of independent "features"
// 2. DIRECTORY STRUCTURE
//
// The project follows a "feature-first" structure. This is enforced by the
// 'required_feature_subdirectories' rule below
//
// flutter_app/
// ├── lib/
// │   ├── main.dart
// │   ├── core/         // Shared code (networking, theme, utils, etc.)
// │   └── features/
// │       └── [feature_name]/
// │           ├── data/
// │           │   ├── datasources/
// │           │   ├── models/
// │           │   └── repositories/
// │           ├── domain/
// │           │   ├── entities/
// │           │   ├── repositories/
// │           │   └── usecases/
// │           └── presentation/
// │               ├── bloc/ or cubit/
// │               ├── pages/
// │               └── widgets/
// ├── test/             // Mirrors the lib/ structure for unit/widget tests
// └── .cursorrules
// 3. RECOMMENDED THIRD-PARTY LIBRARIES
//
// To maintain consistency and leverage powerful, community-vetted tools, this
// project recommends the following libraries for specific tasks
//
// - State Management: flutter_bloc / bloc
// - Why: Predictable state management that separates business logic from UI
// - Usage: Use Cubit for simple state, Bloc for complex, event-driven state
//
// - Routing: go_router
// - Why: A declarative routing package that simplifies navigation, deep linking
//   and passing arguments while reducing boilerplate. Maintained by the Flutter team
//
// - Dependency Injection (DI): get_it & injectable
// - Why: `get_it` is a fast and simple service locator. `injectable` is a
//   code generator that automates dependency registration, reducing manual setup
//
// - Networking: dio
// - Why: A powerful HTTP client that supports interceptors, request cancellation
//   file downloads, and global configuration
//
// - Local Storage: hive
// - Why: A lightweight, blazing-fast, and easy-to-use key-value database
//   written in pure Dart. Ideal for caching data and user settings
//
// - Immutability / Code Generation: freezed
// - Why: Generates immutable data classes, unions (for states), and handles
//   copyWith, toJson/fromJson, significantly reducing boilerplate
// 4. LINTING & STRUCTURE RULES
// 4.1. File and Directory Naming Conventions
// Enforce snake_case for all file names to maintain consistency
file_naming_convention: snake_case

// Enforce that feature directories contain data, domain, and presentation subdirectories
// This ensures adherence to the Clean Architecture structure on a per-feature basis

required_feature_subdirectories:

- data
- domain
- presentation

// 4.2. Code Style Rules
// Set a maximum line length to improve code readability
max_line_length: 80

// Enforce that all use cases in the domain layer have a single public method named 'call'
// This creates a consistent API for executing business logic
use_case_public_method: call

// 4.3. State Management Rules (Bloc vs. Cubit)
// Guideline for choosing between Bloc and Cubit
// - Use Cubit for simple state management (e.g., fetching data, toggling a switch)
// - Use Bloc for complex state logic with distinct, traceable events (e.g., multi-step forms)

state_management_guideline:

  prefer_cubit_for_simple_state: true
  prefer_bloc_for_complex_state: true

// 4.4. Dependency Rules (The Dependency Inversion Principle)
// Prevent the domain layer from importing from data or presentation layers
// This is the core rule of Clean Architecture, keeping business logic pure

disallowed_imports:

- from: "package:flutter_app/features/*/domain/**"
    to:
  - "package:flutter_app/features/*/data/**"
  - "package:flutter_app/features/*/presentation/**"
  - "package:flutter/**"
  - "package:flutter_bloc/**"
// Prevent the data layer from importing from the presentation layer
// The data layer should only be concerned with data sources, not UI
- from: "package:flutter_app/features/*/data/**"
    to:
  - "package:flutter_app/features/*/presentation/**"

// 4.5. Testing Rules
// Require test files for all BLoCs, Cubits, and UseCases to ensure high test coverage
// for business logic and state management

require_tests_for:

- "**/*_bloc.dart"
- "**/*_cubit.dart"
- "**/*_usecase.dart"
